	(text "Application Notes\n1)The traces from ANT1 and ANT2 through the matching network to the final output must be as short and straight as physically possible. No sharp 90-degree corners-use 45-degree bends or gentle curves.\n2)The final trace leading out from the matching network to the antenna must maintain a strict 50-ohm characteristic impedance\n3)No signal/ power traces should be routed underneath the RF section.\n4) Keep out zone should be used for the chip antenna"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
